            <div class="arch-index">FOLIA + FLAMEMC / SYSTEM DESIGN</div>
            <h3>Supported calls.<br/>The <span>right thread.</span></h3>
            <p>Instead of pretending there is one universal main thread, FlameMC routes supported legacy operations through their actual owners.</p>
            <ol class="architecture-steps">
              <li><span class="step-num">01</span><div><strong>Plugin code calls the API.</strong><p>Familiar Bukkit and Paper interaction points.</p></div></li>
              <li><span class="step-num">02</span><div><strong>FlameMC applies compatibility.</strong><p>Context-aware routing, scheduling and supported synchronous behavior.</p></div></li>
              <li><span class="step-num">03</span><div><strong>Folia executes on the owner.</strong><p>Region, entity and global ownership remain the source of truth.</p></div></li>
            </ol>
            <p class="architecture-footnote">Supported operations follow their defined contracts; compatibility is not a blanket bypass of Folia thread safety.</p>
