    <section class="section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="container faq-grid">
        <div class="faq-intro" data-reveal><p class="kicker"><span class="kicker-num">05</span> / QUESTIONS</p><h2 id="faq-title">Clear answers.<br/><span class="text-gradient">No magic claims.</span></h2><p>Powerful concurrency needs precise behavior. Here's what the platform actually sets out to do.</p></div>
        <div class="faq-list" data-reveal>
          <details><summary>Is FlameMC based on Folia?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Yes. Folia's regionized threading and ownership model are the foundation. FlameMC builds its compatibility behavior around those guarantees.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Will my Paper plugins work unchanged?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>Many common workflows are targeted by the compatibility layer, but full compatibility is not guaranteed. Plugins that rely on unsupported synchronous or cross-region behavior still need testing or adaptation.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Does region threading guarantee higher TPS?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Independent regions can use multiple cores, but performance depends on workload partitioning, how players are distributed, hardware, and plugin cost. No fixed multiplier is guaranteed.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Does FlameMC disable Folia's safety checks?<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>No. Its design keeps native ownership as the authority and routes compatible operations to the correct executor rather than freely accessing live state from the wrong region.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

